  "question": {
    "text": "If the three lines $x-3 y=p, a x+2 y=q$ and $a x+y=r$ form a right-angled triangle then :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CgOvq",
      "text": "\n$a^2-9 a+18=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNBzD",
      "text": "\n$a^2-6 a-12=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "POZlE",
      "text": "\n$a^2-6 a-18=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UQrzU",
      "text": "\n$a^2-9 a+12=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since three lines $x-3 y=p$, $a x+2 y=q$ and $a x+y=r$ form a right angled triangle $\\therefore$ product of slopes of any two lines $=-1$ Suppose $a x+2 y=q$ and $x-3 y=p$ are $\\perp$ to each other.\n$$\n\\therefore \\frac{-a}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{3}=-1 \\Rightarrow a=6\n$$\nNow, consider option one by one $a=6$ satisfies only option (a)\n$\\therefore$ Required answer is $a^2-9 a+18=0$",
    "image": null
  },
